<!--
  The status-bar icon for push notifications.

  Android 5+ renders a notification's small icon as a SILHOUETTE: every
  non-transparent pixel is painted a flat colour and the alpha channel is the
  only thing that survives. Hand it a full-colour launcher icon — which is
  what FCM falls back to when no default is declared, and what was happening
  here — and the system draws a grey square.

  So this is deliberately one solid shape on transparency, with no gradient,
  no colour and no fine detail: a speech bubble, which reads at 24dp and
  suits an app about people talking. The tint comes from
  default_notification_color in the manifest.
-->
